{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And Melchizedek.</b> For it is the way to bring out [food] to those who come from battle, as they are exhausted and hungry and thirsty. Another explanation: bread and wine alluded to the meal-offerings and libations, for at first he was a priest, as it is said: ״והוא כהן לאל עליון״ — and he lost his priesthood because he preceded the blessing of Abraham before the blessing of the Holy One, blessed be He. Thus it is written: ״נשבע ה' ולא ינחם״ — ״על דברתי מלכי צדק״, that is, concerning the utterance of Melchizedek. And that is what is written: ״והוא כהן״ — he is a priest, but his seed is not priests. Thus it is concluded in Nedarim."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:44.036323725Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}